{#- =====================================================================
    Inovelli VZM31-SN LED bar - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
    =====================================================================

    LED numbering: LED 1 = bottom segment, LED 7 = top.
    Tier -> LED, as implemented in script.led_set (scripts.yaml):
        mode     -> Led 4    spatial -> Led 7
        global   -> Led 1    critical -> All (whole bar)

    WHO READS THIS FILE
      global tier (Led 1)   automations.yaml 'Notification: Apply Global LED
                            on state change' is DRIVEN by global_table() -
                            edit the table here and the bar follows.
      mode tier (Led 4)     automations.yaml 'Notification: Apply Mode LED on
                            state change' is MIRRORED here, not driven. Edit
                            both or binary_sensor.led_4_table_agrees goes off.
      critical tier (All)   automations.yaml 'Notification: Apply Critical LED
                            on state change' is MIRRORED here, not driven.
      spatial tier (Led 7)  scripts.yaml script.cube_room_indicator is
                            MIRRORED here, not driven.
      dashboard             /lighting-status/0, via the sensor.led_* entities
                            in packages/led_status.yaml.

    LEDs 2, 3, 5 and 6 are written by nothing. There is no table for them.

    Macros return STRINGS, so every table emits JSON and every consumer pipes
    it through | from_json. Keep every tag whitespace-trimmed ({%- -%}) or
    from_json will choke on the newlines.

    Excluded by design: ad-hoc whole-bar calls such as the 20 s broadcast
    flash in automations.yaml, which have no persistent state to read.
-#}


{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------- ----
    SWITCH SETS
    The twelve non-sanctuary switches and the four sanctuary ones. The
    sanctuary list is duplicated inside script.led_set, which applies the
    night brightness cap; this copy decides who is TARGETED at all.
-------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}
{%- macro switch_sets() -%}
{
"main": [
"light.family_room_wall_switch","light.kitchen_wall_switch",
"light.awning_wall_switch","light.office_wall_switch",
"light.upstairs_hallway_wall_switch","light.basement_bathroom_wall_switch",
"light.basement_hallway_wall_switch","light.garage_wall_switch",
"light.basement_deck_wall_switch","light.upstairs_deck_wall_switch",
"light.front_porch_wall_switch","light.stairs_wall_switch"],
"sanctuary": [
"light.master_bedroom_wall_switch","light.master_bedroom_closet_wall_switch",
"light.master_bathroom_wall_switch","light.ethan_s_bedroom_wall_switch"]
}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro all_switches() -%}
{%- set s = switch_sets() | from_json -%}
{{- (s.main + s.sanctuary) | to_json -}}
{%- endmacro -%}


{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------- ----
    GLOBAL TIER - LED 1
    Priority order matches the sensor.active_global_notification UI helper
    (.storage/core.config_entries). binary_sensor.led_1_table_agrees checks
    that the two have not drifted.

    ONE COLOUR PER STATE: red is reserved for critical, blue for the
    switch's own firmware default, leaving exactly seven usable colours for
    seven states. Orange and yellow are the one confusable pair, so they are
    additionally separated by effect (front door pulses, fridge slow-blinks).
    Adding a state means picking a new axis, not a new colour.
-------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}
{%- macro global_table() -%}
[
{"p":1,"key":"garage_overhead","label":"Garage Door Open","short":"Garage Door",
 "entity":"cover.garage_door","on":"open","color":"white","effect":"pulse",
 "sanctuary":true,"icon":"mdi:garage-open-variant",
 "why":"The overhead door - the largest exposure in the house."},
{"p":2,"key":"front_door","label":"Front Door Open","short":"Front Door",
 "entity":"binary_sensor.front_door","on":"on","color":"orange","effect":"pulse",
 "sanctuary":true,"icon":"mdi:door-open",
 "why":"Perimeter breach. Pulses so it cannot be confused with the fridge."},
{"p":3,"key":"garage_entry","label":"Garage Entry Door Open","short":"Garage Entry",
 "entity":"binary_sensor.garage_portal","on":"on","color":"purple","effect":"pulse",
 "sanctuary":true,"icon":"mdi:door-sliding-open",
 "why":"The walk-through contact. Split off from the front door so the two no longer share orange."},
{"p":4,"key":"kitchen_door","label":"Kitchen Door Open","short":"Kitchen Door",
 "entity":"binary_sensor.kitchen_door","on":"on","color":"teal","effect":"pulse",
 "sanctuary":false,"icon":"mdi:door",
 "why":"Interior-adjacent, so the bedrooms are left out of it."},
{"p":5,"key":"slider","label":"Slider Open","short":"Basement Slider",
 "entity":"binary_sensor.basement_sliding_door","on":"on","color":"magenta","effect":"pulse",
 "sanctuary":false,"icon":"mdi:door-sliding",
 "why":"Basement slider. Split off from the kitchen door so the two no longer share teal."},
{"p":6,"key":"fridge","label":"Fridge Open","short":"Fridge",
 "entity":"input_boolean.fridge_open_too_long","on":"on","color":"yellow","effect":"slow_blink",
 "sanctuary":false,"icon":"mdi:fridge-alert",
 "why":"Latches only after 2 minutes continuously open, so it is a transient go-close-it alert. Deliberately NOT wired to the house alarm."},
{"p":7,"key":"windows","label":"Windows Open","short":"Windows",
 "entity":"binary_sensor.window_open_group","on":"on","color":"green","effect":"pulse",
 "sanctuary":false,"icon":"mdi:window-open-variant",
 "why":"Usually a deliberate ambient state, so it sits below the fridge."}
]
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Every row whose source entity is currently active, highest priority first. -#}
{%- macro global_stack() -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(out=[]) -%}
{%- for r in global_table() | from_json -%}
{%- if states(r.entity) == r.on -%}{%- set ns.out = ns.out + [r] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- (ns.out | sort(attribute='p') | list) | to_json -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The one row the bar is actually painting, or an empty string for Idle. -#}
{%- macro global_showing() -%}
{%- set s = global_stack() | from_json -%}
{{- (s[0] if s else none) | to_json -}}
{%- endmacro -%}


{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------- ----
    CRITICAL TIER - whole bar
    Mirrors automations.yaml. The firmware layers a whole-bar override ABOVE
    any individual LED, so while this tier is painting, LEDs 1, 4 and 7 are
    still being written but are invisible. That is what hides_individual_leds
    reports, and what the masking banner on the dashboard warns about.
-------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}
{%- macro critical_table() -%}
[
{"p":1,"key":"triggered","label":"Triggered","state":"Triggered",
 "color":"red","effect":"fast_blink","brightness":100,"icon":"mdi:alarm-light",
 "why":"Alarm sounding. Bypasses the night brightness cap - a real emergency."},
{"p":2,"key":"armed_away","label":"Armed Away","state":"Armed Away",
 "color":"red","effect":"solid","brightness":100,"icon":"mdi:shield-lock",
 "why":"Whole bar red so the armed state is unmissable from any room."},
{"p":3,"key":"armed_night","label":"Armed Night","state":"Armed Night",
 "color":"red","effect":"solid","brightness":100,"icon":"mdi:shield-moon",
 "why":"Whole bar red so the armed state is unmissable from any room."},
{"p":4,"key":"armed_vacation","label":"Armed Vacation","state":"Armed Vacation",
 "color":"red","effect":"solid","brightness":100,"icon":"mdi:shield-airplane",
 "why":"Whole bar red so the armed state is unmissable from any room."},
{"p":5,"key":"armed_home","label":"Armed Home","state":"Armed Home",
 "color":"red","effect":"solid","brightness":100,"icon":"mdi:shield-home",
 "why":"Whole bar red so the armed state is unmissable from any room."}
]
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro critical_stack() -%}
{%- set cur = states('sensor.active_critical_notification') -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(out=[]) -%}
{%- for r in critical_table() | from_json -%}
{%- if r.state == cur -%}{%- set ns.out = ns.out + [r] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- ns.out | to_json -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- True whenever the whole-bar override is hiding LEDs 1, 4 and 7. -#}
{%- macro critical_masking() -%}
{{- (critical_stack() | from_json) | count > 0 -}}
{%- endmacro -%}


{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------- ----
    MODE TIER - LED 4
    Mirrors automations.yaml. auto is green SOLID, so LED 4 is never dark on
    a mapped switch - this tier has no empty state.

    WHY DEGRADED BLINKS: orange (hue 21) and yellow (hue 42) are close on the
    Inovelli wheel and at brightness 30 orange desaturates toward amber,
    making solid manual and solid degraded indistinguishable. The blink
    carries the distinction instead of the hue. Do not make degraded solid
    again without also moving one of the two hues.
-------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}
{%- macro mode_table() -%}
{
"auto":     {"color":"green","effect":"solid","brightness":15,"icon":"mdi:robot","why":"Motion automations are running."},
"manual":   {"color":"orange","effect":"solid","brightness":30,"icon":"mdi:hand-back-right","why":"A blocker is on - this zone ignores its motion automations."},
"degraded": {"color":"yellow","effect":"slow_blink","brightness":30,"icon":"mdi:alert","why":"The zone's motion automation is switched off. Blinks so it cannot be read as manual."},
"unmapped": {"color":"off","effect":"off","brightness":0,"icon":"mdi:circle-off-outline","why":"No zone owns this switch, so LED 4 is held dark."},
"unknown":  {"color":"white","effect":"solid","brightness":15,"icon":"mdi:help-circle","why":"Sentinel - the mode sensor is unknown or unavailable."}
}
{%- endmacro -%}

