{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------- ----
    PRESENTATION HELPERS
-------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}
{#- led_set's semantic vocabulary -> a frontend colour word. magenta maps to
    pink, following led_set's own magenta -> Pink decision. -#}
{%- macro color_ui(name) -%}
{%- set m = {'red':'red','orange':'orange','yellow':'yellow','green':'green',
             'blue':'blue','purple':'purple','magenta':'pink','teal':'teal',
             'white':'white','off':'disabled'} -%}
{{- m.get(name, 'grey') -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro color_hex(name) -%}
{%- set m = {'red':'#ff453a','orange':'#ff9f0a','yellow':'#ffd60a','green':'#32d74b',
             'blue':'#0a84ff','purple':'#bf5af2','magenta':'#ff375f','teal':'#40c8e0',
             'white':'#f2f2f7','off':'#8e8e93'} -%}
{{- m.get(name, '#8e8e93') -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro color_dot(name) -%}
{%- set m = {'red':'🔴','orange':'🟠','yellow':'🟡','green':'🟢','blue':'🔵',
             'purple':'🟣','magenta':'🩷','teal':'🩵','white':'⚪','off':'⚫'} -%}
{{- m.get(name, '⚪') -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro effect_label(e) -%}
{{- {'solid':'solid','pulse':'pulse','fast_blink':'fast blink',
     'slow_blink':'slow blink','off':'dark','clear':'cleared'}.get(e, e | replace('_',' ')) -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Quick Reference, generated from the tables above so it cannot drift.
    The hand-written version of this legend had already gone stale. -#}
{%- macro legend_md() -%}
### Reading the bar

LED 1 is the **bottom** segment, LED 7 the **top**. Four tiers write four
different LEDs, and the firmware layers a whole-bar override above all of them.

| LED | Tier | Scope | Empty state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Full bar | Critical (alarm) | All 16 switches | Disarmed |
| 7 | Spatial (magic cube) | The selected room | Not flashing |
| 4 | Lighting mode | Per zone | Never - `auto` is green solid |
| 1 | Global notifications | 12 switches, +4 bedrooms for perimeter alerts | Idle |

LEDs 2, 3, 5 and 6 are unused - nothing writes them.

### LED 1 - global, in priority order

Only the highest-priority active cause is painted; the rest queue behind it.

| | Colour | Effect | Cause |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
{% for r in global_table() | from_json -%}
| P{{ r.p }} | {{ color_dot(r.color) }} {{ r.color | capitalize }} | {{ effect_label(r.effect) }} | {{ r.label }}{% if r.sanctuary %} · bedrooms too, dimmed{% endif %} |
{% endfor %}

### LED 4 - lighting mode

| Colour | Effect | Means |
| --- | --- | --- |
{% for k in ['auto','manual','degraded','unmapped'] -%}
{% set t = (mode_table() | from_json)[k] -%}
| {{ color_dot(t.color) }} {{ t.color | capitalize }} | {{ effect_label(t.effect) }} | {{ k | capitalize }} |
{% endfor %}

Tap a room to toggle its blocker; hold for details.

### Two things that make the bar lie

- **Armed alarm masks everything.** The whole-bar red override sits above
  LEDs 1, 4 and 7 in firmware. They are still being painted, just invisible.
- **Bedrooms are dimmed.** Master Bedroom, Master Closet, Master Bathroom and
  Ethan's Room only ever receive the three perimeter alerts, always at
  brightness 1, and after dark every one of them is capped to 1 regardless.
{%- endmacro -%}
